<title>LATVIA: Latvian 1996 trade deficit rises to 483 mln lats.</title>
<headline>Latvian 1996 trade deficit rises to 483 mln lats.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's 1996 trade deficit rose to 483.0 million lats ($832.9 million) compared with 271.23 million lats in 1995, the statistics committe said on Friday.</p>
<p>The committee gave the figures in real prices, which do not strip out inflation. Annual inflation in 1996 was 13.1 percent.</p>
<p>Figures in millions of lats unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p> LATVIAN TRADE BALANCE  Jan-Dec 1996  Jan-Nov '96   Jan-Dec 1995</p>
<p> Exports		    795.17	  726.6	   688.41</p>
<p> Imports		    1.28 billion  1.13 billion  959.64</p>
<p> Balance		    -483.0	  -403.6	  -271.232</p>
<p>Principal trading partners:</p>
<p>Exports 1996 vs 1995:</p>
<p>Russia  - 22.8 vs 25.3</p>
<p>Germany - 13.8 vs 13.6</p>
<p>Britain - 11.1 vs  9.1</p>
<p>Imports 1996 vs 1995:</p>
<p>Russia  - 20.2 vs 21.7</p>
<p>Germany - 13.8 vs 15.4</p>
<p>Finland -  9.2 vs 10.4</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240 ($ = 0.582 Latvian Lats)</p>
</text>
